{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "I have completed a full source-fidelity review of the entire patent application draft, including all claims, the detailed description, the abstract, the list of numerals, and the briefs for all figures. Every limitation in every claim, every numbered part, and every specific structure, relationship, and variant described in the text has been traced to an exact affirmative passage in the inventor's disclosure materials. The draft is largely faithful to the source and internally consistent, with one critical exception in a figure brief that describes a topologically incorrect arrangement.\n\nMy review identified one critical finding related to disclosure fidelity in the brief for FIG. 7. The brief describes a drawing that misrepresents the physical path of the indicator stem by omitting several key intervening structures that are described in the inventor's disclosure and shown in other figures. This creates a contradiction within the application materials. The provided fix corrects the figure brief to describe a topologically accurate drawing, ensuring that all parts of the application are consistent with each other and fully supported by the inventor's source disclosure. After applying this correction, the application will meet the required source-fidelity and internal consistency standards."}
